  "bodyHtml": "\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\n\t\t<div class=\"entry-content\">\n\t\t\t\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter is-resized\"><img class=\"wp-image-3782\" src=\"/media/archive/7b5ab1dab64db9951c570345700741e1253039aee0dcf3d79428ff08ef822115.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"189\" height=\"189\" loading=\"lazy\" /></figure>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The Guild of Harwich Artists hosted a community-painted Mystery Painting Puzzle as part of the state-wide ArtWeek 2019.  This year’s ArtWeek (April 26-May 5, 2019) presented by Highland Street Foundation and produced by the Boch Center, is an annual award-winning state-wide festival featuring hundreds of unique and creative experiences.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What is a Mystery Painting Puzzle?</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Each painter was given a 3”x 3” photo image to paint on a 6”x 6” stretched canvas panel. The individual painters did not know what the larger image they contributed to, and therefore the mystery. Guild member artists were on-hand with supplies to mentor fledgling artists. As the 96 panels were combined during the day the mystery image was revealed, much like a completed jigsaw puzzle.  Cyndi Williams, Executive Director of the Harwich Chamber of Commerce, offered to hang the completed Mystery Painting Puzzle in the lobby of the Harwich Visitor Center in Harwich Port for all to see.</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped wp-block-gallery-1 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\">\n<li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\">\n<figure><img class=\"wp-image-4452\" src=\"/media/archive/7de48cb530c59c5b66cf5da66496042f5099a89084c0b663c339d167fe87dbbf.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></figure>\n</li>\n<li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\">\n<figure><img width=\"565\" height=\"481\" class=\"wp-image-4451\" src=\"/media/archive/573abd61f974a99e273f12e4b3ee081dea13e22d2b86f22da3edfe0b6304faec.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></figure>\n</li>\n<li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\">\n<figure><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"480\" height=\"629\" class=\"wp-image-4450\" src=\"/media/archive/b238d91a77f2c83db0b5abec091b4d5a720d6f1ff7e19141c1d4bd4a97c5f2d1.jpg\" alt=\"\" /></figure>\n</li>\n<li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\">\n<figure><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"768\" height=\"1024\" class=\"wp-image-4449\" src=\"/media/archive/a2cafb67a985e861d35610b0d30045379d2faefc05ec246450438b0662c830ab.jpg\" alt=\"\" /></figure>\n</li>\n<li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\">\n<figure><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"768\" height=\"1024\" class=\"wp-image-4448\" src=\"/media/archive/950d2112fc89ef1103bfd9653678f9aa5422bdfaf44d1b2ae75d46549b9f07b9.jpg\" alt=\"\" /></figure>\n</li>\n<li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\">\n<figure><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" class=\"wp-image-4447\" src=\"/media/archive/bf9d7f2cbfceffbddc3644287761deb1e4e620a6f0013cf8ab647e814b7c548d.jpg\" alt=\"\" /></figure>\n</li>\n<li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\">\n<figure><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" class=\"wp-image-4446\" src=\"/media/archive/c2ad5af73707567bf66f676d7ddd00f11c74016dba2c29ac0c6b111644b5d6d2.jpg\" alt=\"\" /></figure>\n</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">‘Red River Salt Marsh’ – South Harwich</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Image is based on original acrylic painting by Barbara Hageman, Guild member and creative force behind the 2019 Mystery Painting Puzzle.</p>\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator\" />\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Learn more about the project</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed-youtube wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wPnmmCPx3_w&amp;t=714s</div>\n</figure>\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator\" />\n\n<h2 id=\"tablepress-32-name\" class=\"tablepress-table-name tablepress-table-name-id-32\">Business Sponsors</h2>\n<span id=\"tablepress-32-description\" class=\"tablepress-table-description tablepress-table-description-id-32\">Thank you to the following local businesses and community sponsors for their support of the project:</span>\n\n<table id=\"tablepress-32\" class=\"tablepress tablepress-id-32\">\n<tbody class=\"row-striping\">\n<tr class=\"row-1\">\n\t<td class=\"column-1\">Alecsies House of Pizza</td><td class=\"column-2\">Dr. Pamela Lattimer, MD</td><td class=\"column-3\">Port Framing Gallery</td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-2\">\n\t<td class=\"column-1\">A&amp;W Harwich Port</td><td class=\"column-2\">Ed &amp; Shannon McManus</td><td class=\"column-3\">Staples Orleans</td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-3\">\n\t<td class=\"column-1\">Cape Cod Five </td><td class=\"column-2\">Ellen Ellis Cleaning Service</td><td class=\"column-3\">The 400 East Restaurant &amp; Bar</td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-4\">\n\t<td class=\"column-1\">Cape Cod Tileworks</td><td class=\"column-2\">Gross Street Studios </td><td class=\"column-3\">The Weatherdeck Restaurant</td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-5\">\n\t<td class=\"column-1\">Capeside Kitchen</td><td class=\"column-2\">Harwich Paint &amp; Decorating Center</td><td class=\"column-3\">Villa Roma Restaurant</td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-6\">\n\t<td class=\"column-1\">Cranberry Liquors</td><td class=\"column-2\">Kruddens3 </td><td class=\"column-3\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-7\">\n\t<td class=\"column-1\">Doris Mee - Artist</td><td class=\"column-2\">Leo F. Doherty</td><td class=\"column-3\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator\" />\n\n<h2 id=\"tablepress-31-name\" class=\"tablepress-table-name tablepress-table-name-id-31\">Contributing Painters</h2>\n<span id=\"tablepress-31-description\" class=\"tablepress-table-description tablepress-table-description-id-31\">Thank you to the following members of our community for participating in the Mystery Painting Puzzle event:</span>\n\n<table id=\"tablepress-31\" class=\"tabl